in specific neighborhoods, but we have to reckon with the fact that in a lot of the sprawling US transit just doesn't get you the same access to jobs and opportunities that cars do and the solution to that is really scaling up and creating great transit. But I do think that there is some tension there, and we do have to find ways to roll back the dominance of the automobile in our cities. I think it's interesting to think about the entire network that hooks into the bus. And one of the things you mentioned is that you also have to make the experience of getting to and from the bus easier and integrate that into the system that we're talking about.
那么这在打造一个充满活力且功能完备的公交系统方面扮演了什么角色？说到公共交通，步行体验真的很重要。我的意思是，大多数人在其行程的至少一端都在步行。因此，行人体验实际上就是公交体验。你可以为某人提供一辆班次频繁、速度快且可靠的公交车，

