where conversations have to happen at the community level, where you have to have this conversation about what is the community definition of safety, and sort of not just not assume what the answer is. And then I also think when it comes to equity, fairs are really important. How we pay for transit, how much, and whether people are really being treated equally.
让我举几个例子。所以，在许多公交机构，实际情况往往是较富裕的公交乘客支付的费用更少，因为月票有折扣，而低收入乘客却负担不起 upfront（预先）支付那笔月票费用。因此，他们只能在每次上车时支付2.5美元。

