Right. If you crack down, that just means people aren't going to ride, and it means that they're not going to get to work or to healthcare or make the trips that they need to make. More about making cities better by having better buses after this. One thing that struck me when talking to Stephen is that, you know, we have the technology, we need to make our cities more livable and more sustainable. The problem is, is that we just aren't making the best use of that technology. We talk so much about technological innovation in transportation, when the real innovation that is needed
是治理方面的创新，或是公共流程方面的创新，这样我们就能更迅速地建设公共交通项目。我在书中写到的事情之一，是一个令人遗憾的事实：许多公交专用道项目的构思方式，就像一个高速公路的超级项目，包含多轮设计和数十次公开听证会，最终导致的结果是，要在街道上开辟一条公交专用道可能需要耗时6年、8年甚至在某些

